#AUTO 20
#NEEDED 0
# USB controller + PHY state (issue 109a reconnaissance). Read-only.
#
# Snapshots the USB2 PHY GRF and the USB3 OTG clock/reset state so
# we can see what the bootloader + usb_init left us before tackling
# the device-mode enumeration hang (109b). Decode help is in
# docs/022-usb-device-controller.md.
#
# The GRF and CRU reads are always safe. The DWC3 controller-core
# read at the end is only valid if the USB3 clocks are ungated;
# kernel_main runs usb_init (which must ungate them) before the
# probe, so it should be safe — but it is placed LAST so that if it
# ever does hang, every value above it is already in the log.

LOG USB2 PHY GRF CON0 (OTG port): 0x0C52 = controller-driven, normal
R 0xFDCA0000
LOG CON1 (host port, parked) and CON2 (shared analog / commononn)
R 0xFDCA0004
R 0xFDCA0008
LOG line-state / disconnect debounce filters (red herrings, for ref)
R 0xFDCA0040
R 0xFDCA0044

LOG USB3 OTG clock gates: CLKGATE_CON10 bits 8-10 (0=ungated)
R 0xFDD20328
LOG USB3 OTG reset: SOFTRST_CON9 bit 4 (0=deasserted)
R 0xFDD20424

LOG --- DWC3 core (needs usb3 clocks up; placed last) ---
LOG GSNPSID identifies the DWC3 IP revision
R 0xFCC0C120
LOG DCTL (run/stop + state) and DSTS (device status)
R 0xFCC0C704
R 0xFCC0C70C

LOG USB probe complete
